nvidia_modeset: refuse to load before nvidia has initialized RM

On illumos, nvidia's _init does not start RM: rm_init_rm() runs from
nv_global_init(), which only nvidia_attach() calls (the first attach of the
pseudo node or a GPU). nvidia_modeset's _init -> nvkms_setup() ->
nvKmsModuleLoad() allocates through RM right away. If nvidia is loaded but has
never attached (modload nvidia; modload nvidia_modeset, or a forceload),
RM's g_RmApiList is still zero-filled and the allocation calls through a NULL
pointer:

  panic: BAD TRAP: type=e (#pf Page fault) addr=0 ... pc=0x0
  nvidia_modeset:nvkms_call_rm+40
  nvidia_modeset:nvRmApiAlloc+56
  nvidia_modeset:nvKmsModuleLoad+39
  nvidia_modeset:_init+14e
  genunix:modinstall+8a

(measured on the solnix kernel, illumos-gate ac45d71, no GPU present; with mdb
nvidia`g_RmApiList read all zero and nvidia`nv_rm_initialized = 0.)
Linux does not hit this because nv.c calls rm_init_rm() from module init.

Fail _init with ENXIO and a warning instead, the same check nvidia_uvm's
uvm_start() already makes with nv_rm_is_initialized(). The guard sits before
anything nvkms_setup() allocates, so _init's existing fail path (id space and
soft state) is the whole cleanup.
--- a/kernel-illumos/nvidia-modeset/nvidia_modeset_illumos.c
+++ b/kernel-illumos/nvidia-modeset/nvidia_modeset_illumos.c
@@ -44,6 +44,9 @@
 #include "nvstatus.h"
 #include "nvkms-ioctl.h"
 
+/* nvidia.kmod: RM starts at the first nvidia attach, not at its _init. */
+extern NvBool nv_rm_is_initialized(void);
+
 /*************************************************************************
  * NVKMS uses a global lock, nvkms_lock, taken in the driver entry points
  * when calling into core NVKMS.  nvkms_pm_lock synchronizes clients with
@@ -860,6 +863,17 @@
 {
     int ret;
 
+    /*
+     * nvKmsModuleLoad() below allocates through RM.  Until an nvidia
+     * instance has attached, RM's API table is zero-filled and that
+     * allocation calls through a NULL pointer, so refuse to load.
+     */
+    if (!nv_rm_is_initialized()) {
+        cmn_err(CE_WARN, NVKMS_LOG_PREFIX "nvidia is not attached "
+            "(RM not initialized); attach nvidia (/dev/nvidiactl) first");
+        return ENXIO;
+    }
+
     nvkms_alloc_called_count = 0;
     nvkms_popen_count = 0;
     nvkms_nvidia_major = ddi_name_to_major(NVKMS_NVIDIA_DRIVER_NAME);
